L = lesson(c4, "environment-civic", "Environmental and civic responsibility",
    ["Explain why the citizen must protect the environment and public property", "Describe good practices for waste, water, trees and energy", "Explain the role of the community and of the state", "Link environment to sustainable development"],
    [("text", "The **environment** is everything around us: air, water, soil, plants, animals, buildings and people. Citizens depend on a healthy environment for food, water, health and livelihood, and have a duty to protect it for themselves and for **future generations**. **Sustainable development** means meeting today's needs without damaging the ability of future generations to meet theirs."),
     ("key", "retenir", "Good practices", "- **Waste:** put rubbish in bins, sort it, reduce, reuse and recycle; never throw waste into gutters or rivers.\n- **Water:** keep sources clean, do not waste water, treat or boil drinking water when needed.\n- **Trees:** plant and protect trees; avoid bush fires.\n- **Energy:** switch off unused lights, use clean energy where possible.\n- **Public property:** schools, roads, lamps and water points belong to everyone and must be looked after."),
     ("text", "**Community action:** clean-up days, tree-planting, neighbourhood drainage clearing, school environment clubs and awareness campaigns. **The state** makes environmental laws, creates protected areas, provides waste collection and water services and educates the public. Citizens help by following the law, reporting damage and taking part in community action."),
     ("key", "pieges", "Common mistakes", "- 'The government will clean it' is not enough: each person produces waste and must act responsibly.\n- Blocked gutters cause floods; throwing plastic in them is dangerous, not harmless.\n- Burning waste pollutes the air and is not a good way of getting rid of it.\n- Sustainable development is not only about nature: it includes people's well-being and the economy."),
     ("key", "retenir", "Link with health", "A dirty environment spreads diseases: poor waste disposal attracts rats and flies and blocks drains where mosquitoes breed; unsafe water causes cholera and typhoid. A clean environment protects health and saves money.")],
    [("Example 1: practical action", "Name three things a school can do to keep its environment clean.", ["Provide bins and teach pupils to use them.", "Organise regular clean-up days and sort waste.", "Plant trees and flowers and keep drains clear."], "Bins and sorting, clean-up days, trees and clear drains."),
     ("Example 2: cause and effect", "Explain how throwing plastic into a gutter can cause flooding.", ["Plastic blocks the gutter and the flow of water.", "During heavy rain water cannot drain and overflows.", "Houses and roads are flooded."], "Blocked drains cause water to overflow during heavy rain.")],
    (fig, "Three ways to reduce waste", "Three circles labelled reduce, reuse and recycle."),
    [MCQ("Sustainable development means", "Meeting present needs without harming future generations", ["Using everything now", "Stopping all development", "Moving to cities"], "That is the standard definition."),
     TF("Throwing rubbish into gutters can cause floods.", True, "Blocked gutters overflow."),
     MATCH("Match each practice with its benefit.", [("Planting trees", "Protects soil and cleans the air"), ("Sorting waste", "Makes recycling easier"), ("Clearing drains", "Reduces flooding")], "These actions have clear benefits."),
     MCQ("Which action protects public property?", "Reporting damage to the authorities", ["Writing on walls", "Breaking street lamps", "Selling school desks"], "Citizens must care for common property.", tier="approfondissement"),
     OPEN("Explain how a community can protect its water source.", "Keep animals and waste away from the source, avoid washing or defecating near it, build a fence or cover, organise regular cleaning and treat the water if needed.", "1 mark for each of three actions with explanation.", points=3, tier="approfondissement"),
     PROB("In a neighbourhood the drains are blocked with rubbish and the water point is dirty. Children often have diarrhoea.",
          [("mcq", "The main reason for the children's illness may be", "unsafe water and poor hygiene", ["too much sleep", "too much sport", "cold weather"], "Dirty water spreads diseases.", {}),
           ("tf", "A community clean-up could help.", True, "It removes waste and improves health.", {}),
           ("mcq", "Who should act?", "Residents and local authorities together", ["Nobody", "Only children", "Only tourists"], "Both citizens and authorities have roles.", {}),
           ("open", "Suggest two actions to improve the situation.", "Clear the drains, set up a rubbish collection system, clean and protect the water point, teach hygiene and hand washing.", "1 mark each for two sensible actions.", {})])],
    [("The 3 R's stand for", "Reduce, reuse, recycle", ["Read, write, run", "Rest, relax, repeat", "Rain, river, road"], "These are ways of cutting waste."),
     ("Burning waste", "Pollutes the air", ["Cleans the air", "Is always safe", "Makes soil fertile"], "Burning produces smoke and harmful gases."),
     ("Future generations are", "People who will live after us", ["Our grandparents", "Our teachers only", "Foreigners"], "We must protect the environment for them."),
     ("Public property belongs to", "Everyone", ["The mayor alone", "Nobody", "One family"], "It is for the community."),
     ("Trees help to", "Protect soil and provide shade", ["Cause erosion", "Block rivers", "Spread pollution"], "Trees protect the environment.")],
    ["Teacher to verify health statements about water-related diseases and local environmental laws. The examples are general."])

