L = lesson(c4, "road-safety", "Road safety",
    ["Explain why road safety matters", "State the main causes of road accidents", "Describe the rules for pedestrians, cyclists, motorcyclists and drivers", "State basic steps to take at an accident scene"],
    [("text", "Road accidents injure and kill many people and cause great suffering and economic loss. Road safety is the responsibility of all road users: pedestrians, cyclists, motorcyclists and drivers, as well as the authorities who build roads, set rules and enforce them. Most accidents are **caused by human behaviour** and can be prevented."),
     ("key", "retenir", "Main causes of accidents", "**Speeding**; **drink-driving** and driving when tired; **using a phone** while driving; **overloading** vehicles and carrying too many passengers; **poor vehicle maintenance** (bad brakes and tyres); **ignoring signs, lights or the right of way**; **poor roads** and lack of lighting; and **bad weather** with unsuitable driving."),
     ("key", "methode", "Safe behaviour", "- **Pedestrians:** use pavements, cross at crossings after looking right and left, stay alert and do not use phones while crossing; wear light-coloured clothes at night.\n- **Motorcyclists and passengers:** wear a **helmet**, obey the rules, do not overload.\n- **Drivers:** respect speed limits and signs, wear a **seat belt**, check the vehicle, never drive after drinking alcohol.\n- **Everyone:** obey traffic lights and police signals."),
     ("text", "**Road signs** are of three main kinds: **warning signs** (usually triangular), **regulatory or prohibitory signs** (usually round) and **information signs** (usually rectangular or square). Learn the meaning of common signs, such as stop, no entry, speed limit, pedestrian crossing and school ahead."),
     ("key", "attention", "At an accident scene", "Stay calm and make the area safe (warn other drivers); **call for help** from the emergency services; do not move seriously injured people unless there is immediate danger; give simple first aid if you are trained, such as stopping heavy bleeding; stay until help arrives. Check the emergency numbers with your teacher.")],
    [("Example 1: identify the cause", "A bus overturns after taking too many passengers on a bad road at high speed. Identify two causes.", ["Overloading makes the vehicle unstable.", "High speed makes it hard to control on a poor road.", "Both are human factors that could have been avoided."], "Overloading and speeding (plus a poor road)."),
     ("Example 2: pedestrian rules", "Describe how to cross the road safely at a pedestrian crossing without lights.", ["Stop at the edge and look right and left.", "Wait until vehicles have stopped or there is a safe gap.", "Cross quickly without running and keep watching traffic."], "Stop, look both ways, wait for a safe gap, then cross.")],
    (fig, "Traffic light colours", "A traffic light with red, yellow and green lamps and their meanings."),
    [MCQ("A red traffic light means", "Stop", ["Go", "Speed up", "Honk the horn"], "Red means stop."),
     TF("Wearing a helmet on a motorbike reduces the risk of serious head injury.", True, "Helmets protect the head."),
     MATCH("Match each sign shape to its usual meaning.", [("Triangle", "Warning"), ("Circle", "Instruction or prohibition"), ("Rectangle", "Information")], "These are the three kinds of signs."),
     MCQ("Which is a major cause of accidents?", "Speeding", ["Wearing a helmet", "Using a seat belt", "Driving slowly with care"], "Speed is a leading cause.", tier="approfondissement"),
     OPEN("State three ways of reducing road accidents.", "Respect speed limits, avoid overloading, wear seat belts and helmets, maintain vehicles, never drive after drinking, educate road users and improve roads and lighting.", "1 mark each for three ways with explanation.", points=3, tier="approfondissement"),
     PROB("A motorbike taxi carries three passengers without helmets at night on a road without lights. It hits a pothole.",
          [("mcq", "Which factor made the accident more serious?", "No helmets and overloading", ["Using a helmet", "Driving slowly", "A clear road"], "Missing helmets and overloading increase injuries.", {}),
           ("tf", "Bad roads can contribute to accidents.", True, "Potholes and darkness make accidents more likely.", {}),
           ("mcq", "What should a witness do first?", "Make the scene safe and call for help", ["Leave quickly", "Take photos only", "Move all victims immediately"], "Safety and calling help come first.", {}),
           ("open", "Give two things the authorities can do to reduce accidents.", "Repair roads and install lighting, enforce speed and helmet laws, inspect vehicles, and educate road users.", "1 mark each for two measures.", {})])],
    [("Pedestrians should cross the road at", "A pedestrian crossing", ["Any dark place", "A bend", "A bridge only"], "Crossings are safer."),
     ("A seat belt", "Reduces injuries in a crash", ["Increases injuries", "Is only for decoration", "Reduces speed"], "Seat belts save lives."),
     ("Drink-driving is", "Dangerous and illegal", ["Safe", "Recommended", "Required"], "Alcohol impairs driving."),
     ("A warning sign is usually", "Triangular", ["Circular", "Rectangular", "Oval"], "Warning signs are triangles."),
     ("Overloading a vehicle", "Makes accidents more likely", ["Makes it faster", "Makes it safer", "Has no effect"], "Overloaded vehicles are unstable.")],
    ["Teacher to verify against the current highway code and traffic law: sign shapes and colours, helmet and seat-belt rules, and the emergency telephone numbers (deliberately not given)."])

